are orphans without you, Savcı.

265
00:51:37,239 --> 00:51:43,879
But don't worry. Their prayers
are always with you.

266
00:51:47,197 --> 00:51:51,197
May you rest in heaven.

267
00:51:51,197 --> 00:51:56,097
Your son is united with your husband
in heaven, my daughter.

268
00:51:56,601 --> 00:52:00,601
You are a Muslim who is
honored with Islam...

269
00:52:00,601 --> 00:52:04,761
and forgiven for her past sins.

270
00:52:06,568 --> 00:52:10,568
You will join them one day.

271
00:52:11,948 --> 00:52:19,268
Thank Allah that Allah is gathering
you in his heaven.

272
00:52:19,800 --> 00:52:26,380
This earth is short-lasting, my daughter.
The other life is what's important.

273
00:52:28,838 --> 00:52:33,918
Those who win the other life can't lose.

274
00:53:01,480 --> 00:53:12,880
Let's farewell the honorable son of Kayı,
ghazi and martyr Savcı Bey.

275
00:53:13,937 --> 00:53:17,937
With the name of Allah.

276
00:53:18,034 --> 00:53:20,204
Come on.

277
00:53:38,099 --> 00:53:41,419
With the name of Allah.

278
00:54:16,235 --> 00:55:26,467
Allahu Akbar! Allahu Akbar!
Allahu Akbar! La ilahe İllallah!

279
00:55:26,467 --> 00:55:32,277
He gives you fire from the wet tree...

280
00:55:32,277 --> 00:55:37,877
and you set fire with it.

281
00:55:37,877 --> 00:55:42,717
As Allah who created the earth and
the sky created them...

282
00:55:42,717 --> 00:55:47,268
can't he resurrect people too?

283
00:55:47,268 --> 00:55:51,468
Of course, he can! Because he can
create again and again.

284
00:55:51,468 --> 00:55:53,908
He knows everything.

285
00:55:53,908 --> 00:55:59,708
When he wants to create something,
he only says ''Exist!''...

286
00:55:59,708 --> 00:56:03,708
And the thing starts existing
at once.

287
00:56:03,708 --> 00:56:07,188
Allah has a reign over everything...

288
00:56:07,188 --> 00:56:09,418
that lays on earth.

289
00:56:09,418 --> 00:56:12,928
Don't forget that you all will be
summoned before him...

290
00:56:12,928 --> 00:56:16,928
to be questioned.

291
00:56:18,650 --> 00:56:36,323
Reads Qur-an

292
00:56:59,769 --> 00:57:05,859
My beys, you all came here to
share our pain.

293
00:57:06,179 --> 00:57:10,179
-May Allah bless you all.
-Amin.

294
00:57:11,533 --> 00:57:17,003
My sheik, you just said ''He only lacked
a coat''.

295
00:57:17,003 --> 00:57:21,003
-What does that mean?
-Kumral Abdal.

296
00:57:22,115 --> 00:57:29,285
Two beys were paying for the food
that our lodge is giving to people.

297
00:57:30,467 --> 00:57:34,467
One of them is still alive.

298
00:57:35,250 --> 00:57:39,250
Let's not speak his name.

299
00:57:41,179 --> 00:57:46,319
The other was Savcı Bey, my sheik.
He didn't want it to be known.

300
00:57:48,554 --> 00:57:53,514
He had a lot of money.
That's why he was paying.

301
00:57:53,980 --> 00:57:57,400
Is that so, Akça Dervish?

302
00:57:57,400 --> 00:58:04,150
My sheik, he had no store nor any
land nor a wealth of a bey.

303
00:58:05,115 --> 00:58:10,155
He gave everything left from his
wife and children.

304
00:58:13,192 --> 00:58:17,192
My good brother.

305
00:58:18,012 --> 00:58:22,372
He had a horse, armor, and weapons.
Nothing else.

306
00:58:22,372 --> 00:58:27,492
That's what a dervish can have.

307
00:58:46,271 --> 00:58:50,271
Here is a weapon...

308
00:58:50,271 --> 00:58:54,271
drawn for Islam.

309
00:58:55,268 --> 00:59:01,228
Now, this is the legacy
of a great Kayı bey...

310
00:59:02,193 --> 00:59:06,193
to the Kayıs.

311
00:59:08,486 --> 00:59:14,396
This weapon will be given to his
son Ertuğrul.

312
00:59:15,926 --> 00:59:21,686
He will continue the cause of
world order.

313
00:59:22,273 --> 00:59:27,613
With all the other alps who are born
in Kayı Tribe...

314
00:59:28,407 --> 00:59:32,407
he will go to war.

315
00:59:33,741 --> 00:59:37,741
With this weapon.

316
00:59:39,096 --> 00:59:43,976
This cause won't be forgetten.

317
00:59:48,279 --> 00:59:52,669
One of us dies and thousand of us
are born.

318
00:59:53,937 --> 01:00:00,567
Let's leave the Kayı beys alone.

319
01:00:02,078 --> 01:00:05,738
With the name of Allah.

320
01:00:32,024 --> 01:00:37,344
We won a great victory, Osman Bey.
A great victory.

321
01:00:39,181 --> 01:00:45,911
Savcı Bey died seeing and knowing this.

322
01:00:49,458 --> 01:00:54,388
This is my only consolation, Bamsı Bey.

323
01:00:56,815 --> 01:01:01,135
But, this Togay...

324
01:01:01,472 --> 01:01:05,712
why did he retreat from the battlefield,
Osman Bey?

325
01:01:05,808 --> 01:01:10,868
Osman Bey, you seem to know why.

326
01:01:16,497 --> 01:01:23,057
If you want to divide the enemy,
there is a way, Osman Bey.

327
01:01:23,482 --> 01:01:27,952
You will discard one of them from
your enemy list.

328
01:01:33,419 --> 01:01:37,419
You can convince Togay.

329
01:01:40,975 --> 01:01:44,975
Togay? But...

330
01:01:44,975 --> 01:01:48,975
Togay is a heathen Mongol.

331
01:01:50,852 --> 01:01:55,972
The only way to make peace with
the Mongol is to bow down.

332
01:01:59,585 --> 01:02:06,365
Or, making it look like
bowing down.

333
01:02:06,365 --> 01:02:10,365
Bowing down...

334
01:02:12,309 --> 01:02:16,309
becoming a vassal.

335
01:02:16,443 --> 01:02:21,783
However you call it.
That tyrant will believe it.

336
01:02:24,043 --> 01:02:28,733
We won a great victory
with this game, but...

337
01:02:28,912 --> 01:02:35,972
But if tyrant Togay was involved,
we don't know what would happen.

338
01:02:36,738 --> 01:02:44,808
It's one of the first lessons my ghazi
father taught me about war.

339
01:02:46,478 --> 01:02:51,478
Don't fight two enemies at once.

340
01:02:52,397 --> 01:02:58,097
We'll destroy both heathens
separately, Osman Bey.

341
01:02:58,097 --> 01:03:04,737
Don't doubt that. No enemy of Kayıs
has died a natural death.

342
01:03:05,575 --> 01:03:09,855
-Thank Allah.
-It won't change.

343
01:03:10,761 --> 01:03:14,761
Now, listen to me well, beys.

344
01:03:14,761 --> 01:03:19,581
After our mourning ends,
we'll lit the fire of jihad again.

345
01:03:19,581 --> 01:03:23,581
-Inshallah.
-Now, get rest.

346
01:03:23,966 --> 01:03:27,966
With Allah's approval, Osman Bey.
Inshallah.

347
01:03:28,560 --> 01:03:32,560
Thank you, Osman Bey.

348
01:04:01,007 --> 01:04:04,147
May Allah bless you.

349
01:04:12,278 --> 01:04:14,988
Thank you.

350
01:04:18,550 --> 01:04:21,630
One day later

351
01:04:28,297 --> 01:04:32,297
May I enter, Lena Hatun?

352
01:04:40,878 --> 01:04:44,248
Come, Bala Hatun.

353
01:05:24,847 --> 01:05:30,567
We came to farewell you.
-May Allah bless you.

354
01:05:35,326 --> 01:05:39,326
May Allah bless you too, Lena.

355
01:05:40,320 --> 01:05:44,320
I will miss your black and
sad eyes.

356
01:05:53,027 --> 01:05:57,027
I was such a trouble for you.

357
01:06:00,058 --> 01:06:05,058
You have my blessing, Lena Hatun.
Give me yours.

358
01:06:05,058 --> 01:06:10,268
What are you saying?
It's yours.

359
01:06:10,642 --> 01:06:15,312
Don't forget us.
Come visit us.

360
01:06:35,856 --> 01:06:37,956
Gonca.

361
01:06:41,556 --> 01:06:46,866
You came elegantly and you
are leaving elegantly.

362
01:06:48,538 --> 01:06:52,948
You left a noble mark in
this tribe, Lena.

363
01:06:52,948 --> 01:06:56,948
-Gonca.
-Thank you.

364
01:06:56,948 --> 01:07:02,778
Hearing this from such a noble
woman like you is honoring.

365
01:07:02,949 --> 01:07:06,069
Thank you.

366
01:07:22,257 --> 01:07:26,257
Forgive me for drawing my sword
against you.

367
01:07:30,292 --> 01:07:34,292
It was my crazy times.

368
01:07:35,719 --> 01:07:39,719
Is it different now?

369
01:07:46,139 --> 01:07:52,139
Our children...
Our children will grow up fatherless.

370
01:07:53,154 --> 01:07:57,154
We share the same fate now, Lena.

371
01:07:57,826 --> 01:08:00,896
Aygül...

372
01:08:01,270 --> 01:08:05,990
-Give me your blessing.
-It's yours.

373
01:08:07,065 --> 01:08:10,005
It's yours.

374
01:08:14,256 --> 01:08:19,576
Kulucahisar isn't far away.
Come visit me.

375
01:08:21,463 --> 01:08:24,973
Don't live us lonely.

376
01:08:24,973 --> 01:08:30,813
Of course, we will.
We won't leave you or my nephew.

377
01:08:39,619 --> 01:08:45,239
I can't stay in this tent anymore.
That's why I leave.

378
01:08:47,979 --> 01:08:53,059
I will miss you, ladies.
I will miss you.

379
01:09:27,197 --> 01:09:33,227
Give me your blessings.
May Allah protect you.

380
01:09:33,562 --> 01:09:36,092
You too.

381
01:10:12,927 --> 01:10:17,967
It's like I was stabbed
in the heart.

382
01:10:21,013 --> 01:10:27,223
I bore many of the mischiefs
of the heathens.

383
01:10:27,223 --> 01:10:32,643
But the heaviest of the betrayal...

384
01:10:36,664 --> 01:10:42,774
the blow that came from the closest
was the heaviest.

385
01:11:07,511 --> 01:11:12,551
Bala. What did you do?
Tell me.

386
01:11:12,551 --> 01:11:15,901
Did you do what I told you?

387
01:11:16,336 --> 01:11:20,756
Food was handed out for
three days, my bey.

388
01:11:20,756 --> 01:11:24,756
The poor was given a hand.

389
01:11:24,756 --> 01:11:28,756
They prayed for Savcı Bey
and you.

390
01:11:36,194 --> 01:11:41,574
Thank you, Bala.
What about Lena?

391
01:11:42,898 --> 01:11:47,868
She went to Kulucahisar safely
with the alps.

392
01:11:47,919 --> 01:11:51,919
Your nephew Ertuğrul is
safe with her.

393
01:11:58,275 --> 01:12:03,665
Mashallah, Bala. Mashallah.

394
01:12:04,838 --> 01:12:09,398
-May Allah bless you.
-You too, Osman.

395
01:12:15,959 --> 01:12:19,959
May I enter, Osman Bey.

396
01:12:27,191 --> 01:12:30,201
Come.

397
01:12:38,578 --> 01:12:43,108
Beys, this is the end of our mourning.

398
01:12:44,111 --> 01:12:49,791
But our pain will always stay
in our heart.

399
01:12:51,064 --> 01:12:58,314
The enemy won't stay idle.
We need to talk about our measures.

400
01:13:02,051 --> 01:13:06,581
Togay still thinks that
you will pay taxes.

401
01:13:07,668 --> 01:13:12,388
Let him come. We set our game.

402
01:13:12,388 --> 01:13:16,678
We broke their alliance
with the heathen Nikola.

403
01:13:16,678 --> 01:13:22,220
Nikola won't stay idle.

404
01:13:22,220 --> 01:13:28,850
He'll do anything to take revenge for
Malhun Hatun's aid.

405
01:13:29,392 --> 01:13:35,102
We can increase the defenses, Osman Bey.
We can send soldiers to Umur Bey.

406
01:13:39,462 --> 01:13:44,312
We won a great victory, but...

407
01:13:44,782 --> 01:13:48,782
it costed heavly.

408
01:13:50,757 --> 01:13:54,757
Let's not give any more casualty.

409
01:13:54,757 --> 01:13:59,717
To protect Umur Bey, we need
a guarantee.

410
01:14:00,435 --> 01:14:04,435
What kind of a guarantee is that?

411
01:14:05,166 --> 01:14:07,356
Togay.

412
01:14:10,202 --> 01:14:14,202
I will go to Togay.

413
01:14:14,202 --> 01:14:18,202
If he wants us to stay a vassal...

414
01:14:18,863 --> 01:14:24,223
then, he'll stop Nikola
from attacking Umur Bey.

415
01:14:27,067 --> 01:14:33,827
What will we do about Süleyman?
No news from Melik. He must be dead.

416
01:14:34,775 --> 01:14:40,145
Melik was going to bring information
from Nikola.

417
01:14:41,124 --> 01:14:45,124
He failed to do that.

418
01:14:45,124 --> 01:14:49,124
They failed to save their lives.

419
01:14:50,420 --> 01:14:53,370
Now...

420
01:14:58,215 --> 01:15:02,215
Süleyman will pay for it.

421
01:15:03,588 --> 01:15:06,278
Isn't that so, Bamsı Bey?

422
01:15:14,276 --> 01:15:21,916
Osman Bey, he will pay heavily.

423
01:15:24,745 --> 01:15:27,985
Don't you worry.

424
01:15:43,412 --> 01:15:47,582
Lord of Bilecik
sent his regard, Lord Nikola.

425
01:15:47,582 --> 01:15:51,642
Lord of Nikea sent 100 of his cavalry,
Lord Nikola.

426
01:15:51,642 --> 01:15:56,192
Lord of Bursa said that he is with
İnegöl.

427
01:16:00,011 --> 01:16:04,011
Do you know why you come here?

428
01:16:07,753 --> 01:16:12,663
Either victory or death!

429
01:16:13,038 --> 01:16:18,578
There is no other option.

430
01:16:22,613 --> 01:16:26,613
Now, get rest.

431
01:16:36,801 --> 01:16:41,791
With the newcomers,
we have 300 soldiers, Nikola.

432
01:16:41,791 --> 01:16:45,791
300 soldiers. Just in three days,
we have a big army.

433
01:16:47,619 --> 01:16:52,129
Everything is ready to strike the Turks.

434
01:16:52,129 --> 01:16:55,549
We are very close now, Nikola.

435
01:16:55,549 --> 01:17:00,129
I can't wait to attack Umur's tribe...

436
01:17:00,129 --> 01:17:04,129
and storm at him.

437
01:17:07,732 --> 01:17:12,672
Osman's mourning will be
our feast.

438
01:17:14,854 --> 01:17:20,324
I wait for his mourning to end.
I will go and ask Osman Bey.

439
01:17:20,324 --> 01:17:24,324
What does it mean to be the
vassal of the Mongol?

440
01:17:24,324 --> 01:17:27,554
What kind of a valiancy is paying
taxes to Togay?

441
01:17:27,554 --> 01:17:31,724
Don't you know Osman Bey, my bey?
Would he be a vassal to the Mongol?

442
01:17:31,724 --> 01:17:36,594
-Haven't you heard it with your ears?
-It's clearly a plan, father.

443
01:17:36,594 --> 01:17:40,974
-Let's not go there like this. Then--
-Then, what, Malhun?

444
01:17:41,514 --> 01:17:47,034
-Then, we'll be embarrassed.
-Is that what you think?

445
01:17:49,974 --> 01:17:55,064
-Do you know what I think?
-Tell me, my bey.

446
01:17:55,064 --> 01:18:00,594
-I'm listening.
-I think that you deserve a punishment.

447
01:18:00,594 --> 01:18:04,594
As you order, my bey.
You have the right to punish me.

448
01:18:04,879 --> 01:18:12,069
It's better for you to go to Engürü,
to your uncle.

449
01:18:12,069 --> 01:18:16,719
To Engürü? What will I do there, my bey?

450
01:18:16,719 --> 01:18:22,409
I should be here.
I should be with you.

451
01:18:26,619 --> 01:18:30,619
Give me whatever punishment you
want in here, father.

452
01:18:30,619 --> 01:18:34,079
Let me be with you,
support you.

453
01:18:34,079 --> 01:18:38,619
It's better if you don't be
with me for a while.

454
01:18:38,619 --> 01:18:44,069
You'll understand it better that you are
opposing me instead of helping me.

455
01:18:44,069 --> 01:18:46,419
This is your punishment.

456
01:18:49,227 --> 01:18:53,797
When I receive the news I'm waiting
for, you'll move.

457
01:20:08,673 --> 01:20:14,313
You can't do this! Osman Bey promised me!
You can't do this!

458
01:20:16,040 --> 01:20:20,040
Osman Bey is a man of his word.

459
01:20:20,040 --> 01:20:25,010
He said that he'll forgive you for
you to bring news.

460
01:20:25,829 --> 01:20:29,829
But you have failed.

461
01:20:32,750 --> 01:20:35,820
Right, Bamsı Bey?

462
01:20:40,484 --> 01:20:44,484
What does that mean?

463
01:20:44,484 --> 01:20:50,314
Simon died. The mission that my
bey has given is left unfinished.

464
01:20:52,318 --> 01:20:55,348
Let me go!

465
01:20:55,893 --> 01:20:59,893
You will go.
You will go.

466
01:21:09,841 --> 01:21:15,401
You will go, Petros.
But firstly...

467
01:21:15,401 --> 01:21:22,581
you will pay for Süleyman and Melik that
you killed and stole their names...

468
01:21:24,476 --> 01:21:29,466
and for my hand.

469
01:21:30,385 --> 01:21:35,535
-Then, you'll go.
-How will I pay?

470
01:21:38,936 --> 01:21:42,936
-With this.
-Petros.

471
01:21:43,313 --> 01:21:47,913
You will talk to my injured hand.

472
01:21:56,241 --> 01:22:02,011
Without putting blood on my hand,
let me go, Bamsı Bey.

473
01:22:11,266 --> 01:22:16,306
My blood is halal for you, Petros.

474
01:22:18,037 --> 01:22:22,037
But firstly, pay the price...

475
01:22:22,037 --> 01:22:27,667
then, Cerkutay will take you to
our borders.

476
01:22:28,016 --> 01:22:32,016
Don't you worry.

477
01:23:08,101 --> 01:23:15,431
This is for that child that we named
after Süleyman Shah!

478
01:23:28,530 --> 01:23:34,440
And this is for many of our Alps
that you killed.

479
01:23:38,672 --> 01:23:42,672
Now, you've paid the price.

480
01:24:07,387 --> 01:24:09,947
Son.

481
01:24:32,924 --> 01:24:38,384
When you came to Bamsı Bey's tent,
I didn't like either of you.

482
01:24:42,790 --> 01:24:46,460
I was right.

483
01:25:02,196 --> 01:25:06,196
Say hi to Simon.

484
01:25:46,413 --> 01:25:48,863
Stop.

485
01:26:10,349 --> 01:26:16,749
-What's happening?
-They want revenge for their warriors.

486
01:26:18,062 --> 01:26:22,062
They should think about
their own lives.

487
01:26:47,037 --> 01:26:49,137
Stop!

488
01:26:53,515 --> 01:26:58,275
-My bey.
-Göktuğ.

489
01:26:59,945 --> 01:27:03,445
Stay here.

490
01:28:12,641 --> 01:28:16,951
Now, you are here.

491
01:28:17,781 --> 01:28:23,861
You finally bowed down to Ilkhaganetei
to khan of khans, Geyhatu.

492
01:28:24,612 --> 01:28:28,612
Or, have you come here...

493
01:28:28,612 --> 01:28:32,612
to ask for something in return?

494
01:28:34,757 --> 01:28:38,757
We made a deal.

495
01:28:38,757 --> 01:28:44,257
If one of us changes his mind...

496
01:28:44,257 --> 01:28:46,987
everything will be ruined.

497
01:28:48,917 --> 01:28:53,937
-Don't you forget that.
-A deal is a deal.

498
01:28:54,194 --> 01:28:58,194
You are a vassal.

499
01:28:58,194 --> 01:29:02,784
-Tax date is coming.
-Its time will come.

500
01:29:03,717 --> 01:29:09,737
Because Malhun Hatun fought
aside me...

501
01:29:10,157 --> 01:29:14,157
Nikola will want to get revenge.

502
01:29:14,157 --> 01:29:17,957
Do you want me to stop him?

503
01:29:17,957 --> 01:29:22,832
Umur Bey and all the tribes in
these lands...

504
01:29:22,832 --> 01:29:27,622
are under my protection.

505
01:29:28,334 --> 01:29:32,334
If they get attacked...

506
01:29:32,334 --> 01:29:36,334
I'll take it personally.

507
01:29:37,079 --> 01:29:41,079
Gökbörü gets its strenght from
its faith, not from its pack.

508
01:29:41,079 --> 01:29:45,079
Its faith becomes the faith
of its pack.

509
01:29:45,079 --> 01:29:49,499
If you don't break that faith,
it will break you.

510
01:29:49,499 --> 01:29:53,889
It will do it without putting its
fangs on you.

511
01:29:54,605 --> 01:29:58,605
Gökbörü who protects its pack...

512
01:29:58,605 --> 01:30:02,605
came here to show its fangs
to me, Togay the Dark Shaman.

513
01:30:06,070 --> 01:30:10,070
How will I trust your word?

514
01:30:10,078 --> 01:30:15,998
Your messenger will bring you
the gold...

515
01:30:15,998 --> 01:30:19,438
and you will see that.

516
01:30:19,438 --> 01:30:23,438
We'll see, Osman.
We'll see.

517
01:30:23,702 --> 01:30:28,772
Be at ease.
If the tribes are under your protection.

518
01:30:29,050 --> 01:30:34,020
Nikola is in my palm.

519
01:30:34,677 --> 01:30:38,677
We'll see.

520
01:31:05,917 --> 01:31:09,917
What did you tell the Mongol, my bey?

521
01:31:09,917 --> 01:31:15,367
He knows what I told him.
But what he doesn't know is...

522
01:31:15,367 --> 01:31:19,067
what I didn't tell him.

523
01:31:47,487 --> 01:31:52,997
-What will you do, Togay?
-After carrying our Geyhatu's orders...

524
01:31:53,310 --> 01:31:57,730
I will rip out Osman's heart
and eat it.

525
01:32:43,517 --> 01:32:50,207
I remember the things we lost
because of my father. How could he?

526
01:32:50,715 --> 01:32:56,275
How could he?
How can one betray his own tribe.

527
01:32:57,082 --> 01:33:01,942
I'm not crying because I love him,
but I'm ashamed.

528
01:33:06,431 --> 01:33:10,431
Some people...

529
01:33:10,750 --> 01:33:14,750
are called by their fathers' names.

530
01:33:15,626 --> 01:33:19,626
Because they don't have
anything else.

531
01:33:19,626 --> 01:33:23,626
They aren't a thing
on their own.

532
01:33:26,599 --> 01:33:30,599
I heard that...

533
01:33:30,599 --> 01:33:34,599
Osman Bey called you Aygül Alp the
Ghazi of Kulucahisar.

534
01:33:35,390 --> 01:33:40,440
You are the leader of the warriors
women of the Kayı.

535
01:33:41,694 --> 01:33:45,864
And for me, you aren't Dündar Bey's
daughter.

536
01:33:50,737 --> 01:33:55,687
-And what am I?
-Aygül the Mad.

537
01:34:01,924 --> 01:34:07,204
And so am I.
They don't know my parents.

538
01:34:10,294 --> 01:34:14,294
When I was a child, they would call me
Cerkutay who was raised by weasels.

539
01:34:14,294 --> 01:34:18,294
Then, Cerkutay the Bandit,
Cerkutay the Commander...

540
01:34:19,815 --> 01:34:24,935
Now, I'm an alp of the Kayı.

541
01:34:26,739 --> 01:34:30,739
But I was always Cerkutay.

542
01:34:34,264 --> 01:34:38,264
Just like you, crazy girl...

543
01:34:39,001 --> 01:34:43,001
You were always Aygül.

544
01:34:43,442 --> 01:34:47,002
And you will remain so.

545
01:34:54,256 --> 01:34:58,256
I never thought you could
speak so smart.

546
01:35:03,336 --> 01:35:07,336
You eased my heart.

547
01:35:08,868 --> 01:35:15,558
Then, I should leave before
ruining it.

548
01:35:20,639 --> 01:35:24,379
Good.

549
01:35:26,065 --> 01:35:31,195
And you...
Nevermind.

550
01:35:36,139 --> 01:35:41,779
And you...
Don't get cold.

551
01:36:13,955 --> 01:36:20,075
-Welcome, Umur Bey.
-Thank you, Osman Bey. Thank you.

552
01:36:20,075 --> 01:36:24,075
But I'm not well.

553
01:36:24,398 --> 01:36:27,828
What's wrong, Umur Bey.

554
01:36:27,828 --> 01:36:31,518
